# Where src/proxy.ts forwards /api/* (local default shown). In Vercel: the Render API URL, no
# trailing slash. Read at request time, so a change needs no rebuild (a new deployment still
# applies it to the running functions).
BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:8000
# Shared secret with the API's PROXY_SECRET (same value; at least 32 characters:
# openssl rand -hex 32). With it, the proxy tells the API the visitor's real IP, so rate limits
# are per visitor and not one bucket for everyone behind Vercel. Leave blank locally.
PROXY_SECRET=
# The visitor IP comes from x-real-ip, which only Vercel (and proxies you control) overwrite.
# On Vercel nothing to set: Vercel sets VERCEL=1 itself. Anywhere else (next start, Docker, another
# host) a client could send its own x-real-ip, so the proxy forwards neither header and logs a
# warning once. Set true ONLY behind a proxy you control that overwrites x-real-ip. Default off.
TRUST_X_REAL_IP=
